Subject: CPMS I03E4 Activation Source Topology Semantic Refinement

@ [refinement_uuid] 41bff9aa-1b49-47b2-846e-f653ffb6303d
@ [source_uuid] bcd3f900-8f3a-4be1-bea5-b4e84d553ee8

& [ActivationTopology] is the immutable set of input bindings units typed dependency edges ownership records shared ledgers gates and disposition for one candidate implementation campaign

& [ActivationUnit] is a bounded authority transition
  + unit_id is A B C D E1 E2 E3 or E
  + canonical_specification_identity and phase policy
  + hard prerequisites and governance predecessors
  + exclusive source and test paths
  + shared-ledger deltas
  + forbidden surfaces and effects
  + requirement proof review satisfaction and lock identities

& [DependencyEdgeKind] is closed
  + hard_prerequisite means consumer meaning or construction is invalid without active predecessor output
  + governance_order means the campaign serializes units for auditability even when compile construction could be independent
  + integration_order means two units touch one shared ledger and must apply successor deltas serially
  + evidence_dependency means a proof consumes exact predecessor evidence without importing runtime capability

& [SemanticOwner] owns meaning in one exclusive module
  + ownership is singular within one topology
  + owner may propose interface and implementation
  + owner cannot issue its own independent review or integration admission

& [IntegrationSteward] owns mechanical shared-ledger application
  + steward validates lease predecessor and allowed anchors
  + steward applies only declared module cfg and re-export statements
  + steward emits a successor identity and delta receipt
  + steward has no authority to alter exclusive module semantics

& [SharedIntegrationLedger] is Cargo.toml Cargo.lock procedure-tool Cargo.toml lib.rs or conformance/mod.rs
  + Cargo ledgers are exclusively mutable by A
  + lib.rs and conformance/mod.rs are serialized declaration surfaces
  + every successor has exactly one predecessor except the initial conformance/mod.rs creation

& [TouchLeaseCandidate] is a non-active proposed permission envelope
  + exact unit active lock predecessor file identity allowed anchors normalized delta budget owner steward and expiry condition
  + status proposed issued consumed refused stale or superseded
  + this formation creates proposed record grammar only and zero issued leases

& [InterfaceReceipt] binds the boundary between owner and integration steward
  + exact module digest feature gate exports imports faults resource limits tests and forbidden dependencies
  + disposition complete challenged refused or superseded
  + only complete reviewed receipts may be integrated under a future active lease

& [ModuleClass] is ingress registry reader obligation proposal review or report
  + each class maps to exactly one source module and focused integration test
  + integration ledgers have class ledger and cannot contain semantic implementation

& [FixtureRecord] is immutable compile-time corpus identity
  + path role byte count digest generator input lineage owner expected use and review identity
  + generated proposal reviewed expectation and observed result roles remain distinct
  + mutable discovery and runtime writes are forbidden

& [GateObservation] states observed passed failed blocked not_run stale or not_applicable
  + exact command environment artifact policy timestamp evidence and authority scope
  + blocked is not failed behavior and compiled is not executed
  + a newer observation is a successor and does not erase the predecessor

& [UnitCompletion] is conjunctive
  + exact canonical input and active phase lock
  + all requirements implemented and verified
  + completion review and satisfaction record
  + source inventory and evidence closure
  + complete required debug release format lint docs audit and host gates
  + any missing conjunct leaves the unit incomplete

& [TopologyDisposition] is formation_only ready_for_unit_A unit_active campaign_blocked campaign_complete stale or superseded
  + current disposition is formation_only
  + only exact active authority may change it

& [CanonicalOrder] is inputs authority snapshot blockers ledgers owners units dependency edges fixtures gates proofs disposition
& [IdentityRule] excludes timestamps host UI messages commentary hidden reasoning and working-tree order from normative topology identity
& [SuccessorRule] any path owner dependency kind feature gate interface fixture execution scope or authority change produces a new preserved source and topology identity
& [AuthorityRule] topology describes how authority could flow but is not itself implementation activation

& [RefinementDisposition] is semantically_closed_for_formation
